{"id":"mahabharata-6-053","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":53,"title":"त्रिपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 53 · Third day: Arjuna routs the Kauravas","summary":{"en":"Arjuna cuts through the Kaurava chariot division with his arrows, and the Kaurava warriors fall like men at the end of an age. The Pandava and Kaurava heroes fight in pairs, and Kshatriyas drop under the shower of weapons.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನ ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಕೌರವ ರಥದಳವನ್ನು ಸೀಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಯುಗಾಂತ್ಯದಂತೆ ಕೌರವ ಯೋಧರು ಉರುಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಎರಡೂ ಕಡೆಯ ವೀರರು ಜೋಡಿಯಾಗಿ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಆಯುಧ ಮಳೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯರು ಬೀಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन बाणों से कौरवों की रथ-सेना को चीर देते हैं और कौरव योद्धा युगान्त की तरह गिरते हैं। दोनों पक्षों के वीर जोड़ियों में लड़ते हैं और शस्त्र-वर्षा में क्षत्रिय गिरते हैं।","te":"అర్జునుడు బాణాలతో కౌరవ రథదళాన్ని చీల్చుతాడు; యుగాంతంలా కౌరవ యోధులు కూలుతారు. ఇరుపక్షాల వీరులు జంటలుగా పోరాడతారు, ఆయుధవర్షంలో క్షత్రియులు పడిపోతారు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனன் அம்புகளால் கௌரவத் தேர்ப்படையைப் பிளக்கிறான்; யுக முடிவு போல் கௌரவ வீரர்கள் வீழ்கின்றனர். இரு தரப்பு வீரர்களும் இணை இணையாகப் போரிடுகின்றனர், ஆயுத மழையில் க்ஷத்திரியர் சாய்கின்றனர்.","ml":"അർജുനൻ അമ്പുകൾകൊണ്ട് കൗരവ രഥവിഭാഗത്തെ പിളർക്കുന്നു; യുഗാന്ത്യത്തിലെ മനുഷ്യരെപ്പോലെ കൗരവ യോദ്ധാക്കൾ വീഴുന്നു. പാണ്ഡവ-കൗരവ വീരന്മാർ ജോടിയായി പൊരുതുന്നു; ആയുധവർഷത്തിൽ ക്ഷത്രിയർ നിലംപതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.53; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो व्यूढेष्वनीकेषु तावकेष्वितरेषु च ।\nधनंजयो रथानीकमवधीत्तव भारत ।\nशरैरतिरथो युद्धे पातयन्रथयूथपान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with the armies arrayed, yours and theirs, Dhananjaya, a mighty chariot-warrior, killed your chariot-division, O Bharata, felling leaders of chariot-bands in battle with his arrows."}},{"n":2,"text":"ते वध्यमानाः पार्थेन कालेनेव युगक्षये ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रा रणे यत्ताः पाण्डवान्प्रत्ययोधयन् ।\nप्रार्थयाना यशो दीप्तं मृत्युं कृत्वा निवर्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Slain by Partha as by Time at the end of an age, Dhritarashtra's men nevertheless fought the Pandavas in the battle with determination, seeking blazing glory, making death their way of return."}},{"n":3,"text":"एकाग्रमनसो भूत्वा पाण्डवानां वरूथिनीम् ।\nबभञ्जुर्बहुशो राजंस्ते चाभज्यन्त संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"With single-minded resolve they broke the Pandava host many times, O king, and were broken in turn in the battle."}},{"n":4,"text":"द्रवद्भिरथ भग्नैश्च परिवर्तद्भिरेव च ।\nपाण्डवैः कौरवैश्चैव न प्रज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"With some fleeing, some broken, and some turning back, among both Pandavas and Kauravas nothing could be made out."}},{"n":5,"text":"उदतिष्ठद्रजो भौमं छादयानं दिवाकरम् ।\nदिशः प्रतिदिशो वापि तत्र जज्ञुः कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The dust of the earth rose and covered the sun, and in it no one could tell the directions or the points between."}},{"n":6,"text":"अनुमानेन संज्ञाभिर्नामगोत्रैश्च संयुगे ।\nवर्तते स्म तदा युद्धं तत्र तत्र विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here and there, lord of the people, the fighting went on by guesswork, by signs, and by names and clans."}},{"n":7,"text":"न व्यूहो भिद्यते तत्र कौरवाणां कथंचन ।\nरक्षितः सत्यसंधेन भारद्वाजेन धीमता ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kaurava formation was in no way broken, guarded by the wise Bharadvaja's son, true to his word."}},{"n":8,"text":"तथैव पाण्डवेयानां रक्षितः सव्यसाचिना ।\nनाभिद्यत महाव्यूहो भीमेन च सुरक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way the Pandava great formation, guarded by Savyasachin and well protected by Bhima, was not broken."}},{"n":9,"text":"सेनाग्रादभिनिष्पत्य प्रायुध्यंस्तत्र मानवाः ।\nउभयोः सेनयो राजन्व्यतिषक्तरथद्विपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men came out from the front of the armies and fought there, with chariots and elephants entangled, O king, in both armies."}},{"n":10,"text":"हयारोहैर्हयारोहाः पात्यन्ते स्म महाहवे ।\nऋष्टिभिर्विमलाग्राभिः प्रासैरपि च संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horsemen were felled by horsemen in the great battle, with bright-edged lances and with spears."}},{"n":11,"text":"रथी रथिनमासाद्य शरैः कनकभूषणैः ।\nपातयामास समरे तस्मिन्नतिभयंकरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"A chariot-warrior, reaching another, felled him in that terrible battle with gold-adorned arrows."}},{"n":12,"text":"गजारोहा गजारोहान्नाराचशरतोमरैः ।\nसंसक्ताः पातयामासुस्तव तेषां च संघशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephant-riders, locked together, felled elephant-riders in crowds, of your side and theirs, with iron arrows, shafts and lances."}},{"n":13,"text":"पत्तिसंघा रणे पत्तीन्भिण्डिपालपरश्वधैः ।\nन्यपातयन्त संहृष्टाः परस्परकृतागसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bands of footmen in the battle felled footmen with javelins and axes, glad and each blaming the other for wrongs done."}},{"n":14,"text":"पदाती रथिनं संख्ये रथी चापि पदातिनम् ।\nन्यपातयच्छितैः शस्त्रैः सेनयोरुभयोरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"In both armies, footmen felled chariot-warriors in the fight, and chariot-warriors footmen, with sharp weapons."}},{"n":15,"text":"गजारोहा हयारोहान्पातयां चक्रिरे तदा ।\nहयारोहा गजस्थांश्च तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then elephant-riders felled horsemen, and horsemen those on elephants; that seemed a wonder."}},{"n":16,"text":"गजारोहवरैश्चापि तत्र तत्र पदातयः ।\nपातिताः समदृश्यन्त तैश्चापि गजयोधिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here and there footmen were seen felled by the best elephant-riders, and those elephant-fighters in turn by footmen."}},{"n":17,"text":"पत्तिसंघा हयारोहैः सादिसंघाश्च पत्तिभिः ।\nपात्यमाना व्यदृश्यन्त शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bands of footmen felled by horsemen, and bands of horsemen felled by footmen, were seen in hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":18,"text":"ध्वजैस्तत्रापविद्धैश्च कार्मुकैस्तोमरैस्तथा ।\nप्रासैस्तथा गदाभिश्च परिघैः कम्पनैस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With banners thrown down, bows, lances, spears, maces, iron bars and kampanas,"}},{"n":19,"text":"शक्तिभिः कवचैश्चित्रैः कणपैरङ्कुशैरपि ।\nनिस्त्रिंशैर्विमलैश्चापि स्वर्णपुङ्खैः शरैस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"spears, colored armor, goads and prods, bright swords and gold-feathered arrows,"}},{"n":20,"text":"परिस्तोमैः कुथाभिश्च कम्बलैश्च महाधनैः ।\nभूर्भाति भरतश्रेष्ठ स्रग्दामैरिव चित्रिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"saddle-cloths, caparisons and costly blankets, the ground, best of the Bharatas, looked adorned as with garlands."}},{"n":21,"text":"नराश्वकायैः पतितैर्दन्तिभिश्च महाहवे ।\nअगम्यरूपा पृथिवी मांसशोणितकर्दमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With fallen bodies of men, horses and elephants in the great battle, the earth became impassable, a mire of flesh and blood."}},{"n":22,"text":"प्रशशाम रजो भौमं व्युक्षितं रणशोणितैः ।\nदिशश्च विमलाः सर्वाः संबभूवुर्जनेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"The dust of the earth settled, soaked with the blood of battle, and all the directions became clear, lord of men."}},{"n":23,"text":"उत्थितान्यगणेयानि कबन्धानि समन्ततः ।\nचिह्नभूतानि जगतो विनाशार्थाय भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Countless headless trunks rose up on every side, O Bharata, signs for the destruction of the world."}},{"n":24,"text":"तस्मिन्युद्धे महारौद्रे वर्तमाने सुदारुणे ।\nप्रत्यदृश्यन्त रथिनो धावमानाः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that very fierce and terrible battle went on, chariot-warriors were seen running everywhere."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततो द्रोणश्च भीष्मश्च सैन्धवश्च जयद्रथः ।\nपुरुमित्रो विकर्णश्च शकुनिश्चापि सौबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona, Bhishma, Jayadratha of Sindhu, Purumitra, Vikarna and Shakuni, son of Subala,"}},{"n":26,"text":"एते समरदुर्धर्षाः सिंहतुल्यपराक्रमाः ।\nपाण्डवानामनीकानि बभञ्जुः स्म पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"those hard to face in battle, with the valor of lions, broke the Pandava divisions again and again."}},{"n":27,"text":"तथैव भीमसेनोऽपि राक्षसश्च घटोत्कचः ।\nसात्यकिश्चेकितानश्च द्रौपदेयाश्च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise Bhimasena, the rakshasa Ghatotkacha, Satyaki, Chekitana and the sons of Draupadi, O Bharata,"}},{"n":28,"text":"तावकांस्तव पुत्रांश्च सहितान्सर्वराजभिः ।\nद्रावयामासुराजौ ते त्रिदशा दानवानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"drove your men and your sons, with all the kings, in flight in the battle, as the gods did the danavas."}},{"n":29,"text":"तथा ते समरेऽन्योन्यं निघ्नन्तः क्षत्रियर्षभाः ।\nरक्तोक्षिता घोररूपा विरेजुर्दानवा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, those bulls of the kshatriyas, killing one another in the battle, smeared with blood and terrible in form, shone like danavas."}},{"n":30,"text":"विनिर्जित्य रिपून्वीराः सेनयोरुभयोरपि ।\nव्यदृश्यन्त महामात्रा ग्रहा इव नभस्तले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having defeated their enemies in both armies, the heroes, great chiefs, were seen like planets in the sky."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततो रथसहस्रेण पुत्रो दुर्योधनस्तव ।\nअभ्ययात्पाण्डवान्युद्धे राक्षसं च घटोत्कचम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your son Duryodhana, with a thousand chariots, advanced in battle against the Pandavas and the rakshasa Ghatotkacha."}},{"n":32,"text":"तथैव पाण्डवाः सर्वे महत्या सेनया सह ।\nद्रोणभीष्मौ रणे शूरौ प्रत्युद्ययुररिंदमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise all the Pandavas with a great army went against the heroic Drona and Bhishma in the battle, subduers of foes."}},{"n":33,"text":"किरीटी तु ययौ क्रुद्धः समर्थान्पार्थिवोत्तमान् ।\nआर्जुनिः सात्यकिश्चैव ययतुः सौबलं बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kiritin went angrily against capable best of kings. Arjuna's son and Satyaki went against Subala's son's force."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततः प्रववृते भूयः संग्रामो लोमहर्षणः ।\nतावकानां परेषां च समरे विजिगीषताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a hair-raising battle began again, of your side and theirs, each eager to win."}}]}]}